cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Fibrosis-Reentry-MS2D (DOX-LBM-GPU): wavelength-aware 2D monodomain benchmark"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "DOX-LBM-GPU / Fibrosis-Reentry-MS2D contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Coucou2016/DOX-LBM-GPU"
url: "https://github.com/Coucou2016/DOX-LBM-GPU"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Open CPU 2D finite-difference monodomain protocol/benchmark aligned with
  λ-modified Mitchell–Schaeffer choices from Villar-Valero et al. (DOX-inspired),
  not a 3D LBM–GPU digital-twin reproduction. Dual VA endpoints (persist≥1000 ms
  and cycle-required) and wavelength-aware verification geometry.
keywords:
  - cardiac electrophysiology
  - Mitchell-Schaeffer
  - monodomain
  - fibrosis
  - reentry
  - reproducibility
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  authors:
    - family-names: Villar-Valero
      given-names: Jose M.
      et-al.: true
  title: >-
    In silico predictions of action potential propagation in doxorubicin
    cardiotoxicity
  journal: The Journal of Physiology
  year: 2025
  doi: 10.1113/jp288819
